## Summary

In Phase 2 of my SOC lab, I built a working Elastic-based SIEM pipeline from scratch: Elasticsearch and Kibana on the Ubuntu SIEM VM, a self-managed Fleet Server, and a Windows 10 endpoint enrolled with Elastic Agent and Sysmon for deep process, registry, and network telemetry. I validated ingestion in Kibana Discover, built a 5-panel dashboard covering event volume, top event codes, top processes, top parent processes, and network connections, and installed Suricata IDS for network-layer visibility.

Along the way I diagnosed and fixed four distinct real-world issues — missing Kibana encryption keys, a Fleet output pointing at the wrong network interface, a stale agent policy cache, and a missing Windows Event Log channel integration — each traced from symptom to root cause using logs and status commands rather than guesswork. Phase 2 transformed the lab from a set of connected VMs into a functioning, telemetry-producing SOC environment, ready for Phase 3.
